            <ArticleTitle>Multifocal cementoplasty and internal fixation as a palliative procedure for skeletal metastases in the foot: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>489.e13-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1053/j.jfas.2010.02.022</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cementoplasty is a well-established intervention for symptomatic control of localized skeletal metastases; however, its use has never been reported for metastases in the foot. We report on a patient with symptomatic skeletal metastases throughout the foot in which cementoplasty, in conjunction with internal fixation, was used to alleviate pain and enable comfortable ambulation.</AbstractText>
